{"id":461,"flavor":[{"games":["Legends: Arceus"],"text":"This species corners prey as a pack, under the guidance of a leader. Weavile displays increased cunning, leading me to speculate that its evolution caused further brain development."},{"games":["Shield"],"text":"With its claws, it leaves behind signs for its friends to find. The number of distinct signs is said to be over 500."},{"games":["Sword"],"text":"They attack their quarry in packs. Prey as large as Mamoswine easily fall to the teamwork of a group of Weavile."},{"games":["Ultra Moon"],"text":"Thanks to its increased intelligence, scrapping over food is a thing of the past. A scratch from its claws will give you a case of frostbite!"},{"games":["Ultra Sun"],"text":"One Weavile will trip a Sandshrew and flip it over, and then another Weavile will deal the finishing blow with its sharp claws."},{"games":["Moon"],"text":"They dwell in cold places. This Pokémon’s main food source in Alola is Vulpix and Sandshrew, which they carefully divide among their group."},{"games":["Sun"],"text":"They travel in groups of four or five, leaving signs for one another on trees and rocks. They bring down their prey with coordinated attacks."},{"games":["Alpha Sapphire","Y","Diamond"],"text":"They live in cold regions, forming groups of four or five that hunt prey with impressive coordination."},{"games":["Omega Ruby","X","SoulSilver","HeartGold"],"text":"It lives in snowy regions. It carves patterns in trees with its claws as a signal to others."},{"games":["White 2","Black 2"],"text":"They communicate by clawing signs in boulders and work together to surround enemies."},{"games":["White","Black","Platinum"],"text":"Evolution made it even more devious. It communicates by clawing signs in boulders."},{"games":["Pearl"],"text":"It sends signals to others by carving odd patterns in frost- covered trees and ice."}],"abilities":[{"name":"Pressure","hidden":false,"description":"Puts other Pokémon under pressure, causing them to e